The {{Nihongo|'''Empire of Nanami'''|七海帝國|Nanami Teikoku}} is an island nation situated in East [[Fosia]]. Located within the [[Nakami Region]], the archipelago lies to the east of the [[Sea of Mitoyagi]], [[Kwangju]], [[Fenia]], and ZZZ, stretching from the waters of the AAA OCEAN in the south to its maritime borders in the north.

To the north, Nanami shares a vital maritime boundary with [[Okaiken]]. As two of the three primary nations comprising the Sanese Archipelago, Nanami and Okaiken share deep historical, linguistic, and cultural ties rooted in their common Sanese heritage. The two countries maintain a highly integrated economic relationship, frequently collaborating in regional trade, entertainment broadcasting, and technology sectors. Despite this close strategic partnership, Nanami has cultivated a distinct national identity and political structure, shaped by its extensive southern maritime trade networks and its unique imperial history.

Demographically, Nanami is the most populated nation in the Sanese Archipelago. The country is distinguished by an exceptionally high rate of urbanization, with approximately 92.4% of its residents living in densely populated urban metropolitan areas. The national territory encompasses numerous islands, the largest of which is [[Nagashima Island]]. Nagashima also holds the distinction of being the largest single landmass in the broader Sanese Archipelago, notably surpassing the geographic footprint of the island of [[Yagikoshu]] in neighboring Okaiken.

Historically, Nanami underwent a profound transformation during the 20th century, evolving from a largely underdeveloped agricultural state into one of the most livable countries in Fosia. Beginning in the mid-20th century, the nation experienced a period of rapid and sustained economic expansion, ultimately achieving the fourth-highest Gross Domestic Product in all of [[Adonia]]. This modern, industrialized economy is heavily sustained by lucrative sectors such as high-tech manufacturing, software development, and the global export of automobiles. Entering the 21st century, the population of Nanami maintains a very high standard of living, characterized by comprehensive universal healthcare, advanced education systems, and a leading human development index rating.

